ld":-0.0009801472476077468,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":10.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.001668016194331984,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":97.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.36041,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.7,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":70.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"GBank Financial Holdings Inc. operates as a bank holding company for GBank that provides banking services to commercial and consumer customers in Nevada. The company offers business and personal checking and savings accounts. It also provides small business administration loans; commercial real estate, equipment, business term, and medical/professional loans; business lines of credit; accounts receivable/inventory financing services; and credit cards. In addition, the company offers business and personal digital banking; debit cards; additional services; Zelle cash; business courier; merchant card; positive pay; and remote deposit capture services. It serves small- and medium-sized businesses, high net worth individuals, professionals, and investors. The company was founded in 2007 and is based in Las Vegas, Nevada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey K. Newgard | President, CEO, Director, Principal Executive & Interim Financial Officer | Age 53","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 179 people. Revenue per employee of $6.9M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $51K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $12K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["GBank Financial Holdings Inc. is a micro-cap financial services business with a $231M market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 10% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $9M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.46\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 36% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 27% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"GBank Financial Holdings (GBFH) Stock Price Faces Q3 Earnings Margin Pressure","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-gbfh/gbank-financial-holdings/news/gbank-financial-holdings-gbfh-stock-price-faces-q3-earnings","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793320547.607,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.681,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Gbank Financial outlines fintech roadmap with Terribles going live in early November as Lucky Loads targets Q2 next year launch (NASDAQ:GBFH)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4659884-gbank-financial-outlines-fintech-roadmap-with-terribles-going-live-in-early-november-as-lucky","date":"2026-10-29","timestamp":1793255522.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","product"]},{"title":"GBank Financial (GBFH) Shares Tumble 30% in After-Hours Trading: Here's Why","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/10/62682579/gbank-financial-gbfh-shares-tumble-30-in-after-hours-trading-heres-why","date":"2026-10-29","timestamp":1793251134.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What GBank Financial (GBFH) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/gbank-financial-gbfh-said-q3-050416292.html","date":"2026-10-29","timestamp":1793250256.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.103,"tier":0,"sc